From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:38:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let the spike's gate tear a sealed log, and open under
 wrong keys

The gate gains stage 3's key check controls: --es seal wrong opens
places', the logins' and autofill's databases each under another's
key, and logs what each open did; and --es keycheck make|read keeps a
sealed places database of its own in the cache, under a key of its own
from the vault's, with visits closed into the database and more left in
its log, so that a check can tear its log and damage its pages between
the two and see what each read does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
